## AUTO-OKAY PROTOCOL

As PM, your ticket clarity directly impacts whether agent PRs can auto-okay (pass through automated approval). Poor tickets create ambiguous implementations that fail code review and block the auto-merge pipeline.

### Auto-Okay Enablement Responsibilities
1. **Unambiguous acceptance criteria**: Every ticket must have binary pass/fail criteria that Code Reviewer (Agent-12) can validate programmatically
2. **Explicit dependency declarations**: Every ticket must list which agents are blocked and in what order
3. **Scope boundaries**: Define exactly what is IN scope and OUT of scope to prevent scope creep that causes review rejections
4. **Auto-okay readiness tag**: Add `auto-okay-ready: true` to tickets that have clear, reviewable acceptance criteria

### Ticket Template Addition for Auto-Okay
Add to every ticket:
```markdown
## Auto-Okay Criteria
- [ ] Acceptance criteria are binary (pass/fail, no subjective judgment)
- [ ] Dependencies explicitly listed with PR numbers when known
- [ ] Scope boundaries clearly defined
- [ ] No human approval gates required (unless security/compliance)
- [ ] Estimated auto-merge window: [N minutes after PR creation]
```

### PM Anti-Patterns That Block Auto-Okay
- Vague acceptance criteria ("make it look good") -- causes review rejections
- Missing dependency chains -- causes merge conflicts
- Scope creep mid-sprint -- causes failed CI checks
- Undeclared compliance requirements -- causes security blocks

